# Answer key for the "airline-ops" gold dataset (Postgres) — HUMAN-MAINTAINED.
# Wave B1.b of Milestone 1.23 (F1.23.4): statistical-power wave.
# Story: short-haul carrier 18 months after a subsidiary merger — FKs re-added NOT VALID,
# ACARS files landing without constraints, the pre-merger crew-hours table still in the schema.
# See ./README.md for the planted-defect table.
#
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"ops","entity":"airports","field":"info_url","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 240 info_url values are internal wiki paths (\"ops-wiki/stations/…\") with no scheme — they fail the url format, so the station-brief link is dead for 5% of stations."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"ops","entity":"airports","field":"country_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: country_cd stored as GB / gb / Gb / \"ES \" ... — 186 raw values collapse to 179 normalized, so per-country slot reporting double-counts seven countries."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"airports","field":"timezone_name","severity":"low","note":"planted: timezone_name is null for 8% (384/4800) of stations — the subsidiary's station list carried UTC offsets only, so local-time arrival reporting silently falls back to UTC for those stations."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"airports","field":"iata_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 12 duplicate IATA codes on the declared UNIQUE key — the subsidiary's station list used private codes for two heliports that collide with real IATA codes already in the table."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"ops","entity":"aircraft","field":"airframe_uuid","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 38 airframe_uuid values are the manufacturer's serial number rather than a UUID — they fail the uuid format and break the join to the maintenance vendor's extract."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"aircraft","field":"home_base_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: home_base_cd is null for 15% (96/620) of airframes — the merged subsidiary's fleet was loaded before base assignments were agreed, so crew-positioning cost is unallocated for those tails."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"aircraft","field":"retired_on","severity":"medium","note":"planted: retired_on carries a 2099-12-31 sentinel for \"still in service\" — a future date in the column fleet-planning reads to compute remaining life."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"aircraft","field":"tail_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 4 duplicate tail numbers on the declared UNIQUE key — re-registered airframes were inserted as new rows instead of updated, so two rows claim the same registration."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"flights","field":"service_type_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: service_type_cd is null on 12% (2208000/18400000) of flights — the subsidiary's schedule feed never carried it, so charter-vs-scheduled splits exclude a whole fleet."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"flights","field":"flight_key","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 9400 duplicate flight_key values (carrier + number + date) on the declared UNIQUE key — the merged subsidiary's flights were loaded twice for the overlap month."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"flight_legs","field":"delay_code_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: delay_code_id is null on 72% (30240000/42000000) of legs — on-time legs are left uncoded, but so are the delayed legs the ops centre never triaged, and the two cases are indistinguishable in this column."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"flight_legs","field":"fuel_burn_kg","severity":"low","note":"planted: fuel_burn_kg reaches -840 — the ACARS uplift/burn difference goes negative when a tanker leg refuels mid-turn, and the sign error propagates into the fuel-efficiency KPI."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"maintenance_orders","field":"work_package_cd","severity":"medium","note":"planted: work_package_cd is null on 20% (172000/860000) of orders — line-maintenance defects raised by the crew are opened without a package, so unscheduled work cannot be costed."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"maintenance_orders","field":"downtime_hours","severity":"low","note":"planted: downtime_hours reaches -6 — the release-to-service timestamp is occasionally stamped before the grounding timestamp, producing negative downtime in availability reporting."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"maintenance_orders","field":"start_at, end_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: the whole end_at range (2018-09-14 … 2025-11-02) precedes the whole start_at range (2019-02-01 … 2026-08-09) — the merged subsidiary's work orders were mapped with the two columns transposed."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"delay_codes","field":"owner_team","severity":"medium","note":"planted: owner_team is null for 15% (51/340) of delay codes — codes inherited from the subsidiary were never assigned an accountable team, so those delays appear in no team's scorecard."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"ops","entity":"delay_codes","field":"revised_on","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest revised_on is 2023-06-30 (1139 days stale) — IATA revised the delay-code list twice since, so every code introduced after mid-2023 lands as an unmapped value in ops reporting."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"v_aircraft_status","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view is specified as one row per airframe, but the join to the open-defect list fans out and leaves 8 duplicate aircraft_id values — fleet availability is over-counted by every consumer that counts rows."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"v_aircraft_status","field":"utilisation_pct","severity":"medium","note":"planted: utilisation_pct maxes at 143.2 in a column named as a percentage — block hours are divided by a planned-hours denominator that excludes wet-leased days."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"ops","entity":"v_aircraft_status","field":"last_flown_at","severity":"low","note":"planted: last_flown_at is null for 7% (42/620) of airframes — tails that have not flown since the merger cutover are indistinguishable from tails that flew today."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_acars_feed","field":"leg_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 183200 duplicate leg_id values in the ACARS landing table — the datalink provider re-sends a whole day whenever an acknowledgement is missed, and nothing de-duplicates before the merge."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_acars_feed","field":"sched_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 96000 sched_date values arrive as DDMMMYY (\"14AUG26\"), the ACARS wire format, instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format and parse as null downstream."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_acars_feed","field":"block_minutes","severity":"low","note":"planted: block_minutes uses -999 as the datalink provider's \"not reported\" sentinel — a negative in a duration column that any aggregate reads as a real value."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_acars_feed","field":"event_ts","severity":"medium","note":"planted: event_ts reaches 2087-06-30 — a handful of aircraft clocks are set to the wrong decade after a battery change, and the out-of-range timestamps survive the load."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_aircraft_master","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 6 duplicate aircraft_id values in the master landing table — the subsidiary extract and the parent extract overlap on the six airframes transferred mid-year."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_aircraft_master","field":"delivery_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 44 delivery_date values are the string \"TBC\" written by the extract for airframes on order — they fail the date-string format."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: contact_email is null for 12% (2880/24000) of crew — the subsidiary's HR extract carried only internal mail aliases, so disruption notifications never reach them."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"contact_email","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 410 contact_email values are malformed (internal alias with no domain, e.g. \"j.okonkwo@\") — they fail the email format."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"mobile_number","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 620 mobile_number values still carry the legacy roster system's placeholders (\"NO MOBILE\", \"SEE CREW CONTROL\") — they fail the phone format, so standby call-outs silently skip them."}
{"dimension":"consistency","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"rank_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: rank_cd stored as CPT / cpt / Cpt / FO / fo ... — 16 raw values collapse to 11 normalized, so seniority reporting splits the same rank across rows."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"base_cd","severity":"low","note":"planted: base_cd is null for 7% (1680/24000) of crew — crew on long-term secondment lost their base on the merge, and rostering treats \"no base\" as \"any base\"."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"crew","entity":"crew_members","field":"employee_no","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 180 duplicate employee_no values on the declared UNIQUE key — the subsidiary's employee numbering restarted at 1, so 180 numbers now belong to two people."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"rosters","field":"flight_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: flight_id is null on 20% (1240000/6200000) of roster rows — standby, training and leave duties carry no flight, but so do 40000 flying duties the merge failed to link, and the column cannot tell them apart."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"qualifications","field":"issuing_authority","severity":"medium","note":"planted: issuing_authority is null on 15% (27000/180000) of qualifications — subsidiary-issued ratings were migrated without their authority, so licence-validity checks against the regulator cannot be automated."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"training_records","field":"score_pct","severity":"low","note":"planted: score_pct is null on 9% (84600/940000) of records — pass/fail-only courses legitimately have no score, but so do 12000 scored courses whose result never came back from the training provider."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"crew","entity":"training_records","field":"completed_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: completed_on reaches back to 1800-01-01 — the subsidiary's training system wrote its minimum date for records imported from paper, so \"oldest training record\" is meaningless."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"crew","entity":"stg_roster_import","field":"roster_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 21600 duplicate roster_id values in the landing table — the rostering vendor's nightly file overlaps the previous night by 24 hours by design, and the merge does not de-duplicate."}
{"dimension":"validity","namespace":"crew","entity":"stg_roster_import","field":"duty_date","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 18400 duty_date values arrive as MM/DD/YYYY from the vendor's US region instead of ISO — they fail the date-string format, and the ambiguous ones parse to the wrong day rather than failing loudly."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"crew","entity":"legacy_crew_hours","field":"crew_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: crew_id is the natural key of this monthly-hours table and carries 8400 duplicate rows — the subsidiary's system re-issued a full history whenever a correction was filed, so totals double-count."}
{"dimension":"reasonability","namespace":"crew","entity":"legacy_crew_hours","field":"worked_on","severity":"low","note":"planted: worked_on reaches back to 1899-12-30 — the spreadsheet epoch, written by the original loader wherever the duty date was blank."}
{"dimension":"timeliness","namespace":"crew","entity":"legacy_crew_hours","field":"reported_at","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the newest reported_at is 2024-01-31 (924 days stale) — the subsidiary's hours system was retired at the merger, but two fatigue-risk reports still read from this table and silently show pre-merger data."}
{"dimension":"uniqueness","namespace":"crew","entity":"v_crew_currency","field":"crew_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the currency view is specified as one row per crew member, but crew holding two type ratings appear twice — 360 duplicate crew_id values, so \"crew current on type\" is over-reported."}
{"dimension":"completeness","namespace":"crew","entity":"v_crew_currency","field":"days_to_expiry","severity":"low","note":"planted: days_to_expiry is null for 8% (1920/24000) of crew — those with no recorded expiry date, which the view renders identically to crew with no upcoming expiry."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"flights","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 24000 flights reference an aircraft_id with no aircraft row — airframes returned to the lessor were deleted rather than retired, taking their history's parent with them."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"flights","field":"origin_airport_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 1800 flights depart from an airport_id that no longer exists — stations closed after the merger were purged from the station list."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"flight_legs","field":"flight_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 96000 legs have no parent flight — cancelled flights are deleted by the schedule sync while their flown legs remain."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"maintenance_orders","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 3100 maintenance orders reference a deleted airframe, so the cost of work done on returned aircraft cannot be attributed."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"crew","entity":"rosters","field":"crew_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 18400 roster rows reference a crew_id with no crew_members row — leavers were hard-deleted under the retention policy while their historic duties stayed."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"crew","entity":"rosters","field":"flight_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 42000 roster rows point at a flight that no longer exists — the cross-schema FK was left NOT VALID after the schedule purge."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"crew","entity":"qualifications","field":"crew_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 2400 qualifications belong to a crew_id that was deleted — licence history with no holder."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"crew","entity":"training_records","field":"crew_id","severity":"high","note":"planted: 9800 training records reference a deleted crew member, so completion rates are computed over a denominator that no longer matches the roster."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"flight_legs","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 12400 legs carry an aircraft_id with no matching airframe — no FK was ever declared on the leg-level tail column, so the sub-charter placeholder ids were never rejected."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"maintenance_orders","field":"airport_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 640 maintenance orders name a station that is not in the station list — vendor-supplied line-station codes were loaded verbatim."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"v_aircraft_status","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the status view carries 8 aircraft_id values with no airframe row — it reads the staging table, which still holds tails deleted from the fleet."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"ops","entity":"stg_aircraft_master","field":"aircraft_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 14 rows in the master landing table reference airframes that were deleted between the extract and the load."}
{"dimension":"integrity","namespace":"crew","entity":"stg_roster_import","field":"roster_id","severity":"medium","note":"planted: 31000 landing rows reference roster ids that were re-generated by the vendor after the file was cut, so the merge silently drops them."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"ops","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on ops.ops_incident_vault (safety reports held under a restricted just-culture policy) — 1 of 10 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
{"dimension":"accessibility","namespace":"crew","severity":"medium","note":"planted: the readiness role has no SELECT on crew.crew_medical (occupational-health records) — 1 of 8 tables locked, so the namespace aggregates to ONE medium (partial) finding."}
